    pharm: "1. STOP Vancomycin (no MRSA identified, no indications for ongoing MRSA coverage). 2. De-escalate Meropenem: Transition to a narrower-spectrum, penicillin-based regimen. OPTIONS: IV Benzylpenicillin 4 million units q4h (narrowest, most targeted, and penicillin-susceptible S. pneumoniae). OR IV Amoxicillin/Clavulanate 1.2g q8h (broader, but better oral step-down option). 3. If clinically stable and tolerating oral: Step down to oral Amoxicillin 1g TID or Amoxicillin/Clavulanate 625mg TID to complete 7-day course (4 days remaining). 4. Duration: 7 days total (from day 1 of effective therapy) — current evidence supports shorter courses for CAP if clinical improvement. 5. No role for continued broad-spectrum therapy when directed therapy is available.",
